A||||4||Luni420||Distributor and Timing Questions||||1||
Z||000000||Luni420||11-17-2001||10:34 PM||||Ok so me and my buddy were messing around with his Fiero and we were wondering why it was missing and we looked at the electrical system. We found the rotor and cap were pretty shredded so we got a new cap, wires, and rotor and put them on. We are pretty sure that we got the wiring pattern right but we cant find his book and we cant find a distributor diagram that shows what cylinders on the engine are what number where they lie in conjunction with the distributor cap. We just pretty much replaced wire for wire one at a time so we are not sure. Now this thing didnt run quite right at first and we suspected ignition timing in addition to the tuneup we did. We got a timing light and were gonna do it but we couldnt find the bolt or clamp or whatever holds the distributor in place so we can twist it to get the timing right. Does anyone have any info on this or some links to some helpful diagrams? Any help would be appreciated. Its an 88 GT 2.8 V6.||||reg||1
Z||000001||reddog||11-17-2001||11:11 PM||||I just posted a similar question a few days ago. Here is what I recieved. the 2 connectors are facing to the left rear towards the trunk.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PlugW_1.jpg"> <BR>The distributor bolt is directly under the distributor. It's very hard to see due to the coil and tach filter. BTW you'll need a long extension and a universal extention to reach the little Bastard.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Hope this helps Good luck!!!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Luni420||11-18-2001||12:36 AM||||Dude thanks a million. I think thats what my prob is. We just put the wires on wrong Im pretty damn sure of it. That is perfect. Thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000003||camon||11-18-2001||12:41 AM||||what reddog said!!!!!<P>However I didn't use an extension and a univeral extension to get to it. I used a regular wrench (not sure of the size anymore) to get the distribitor adjuster loose and tight (seemed to work pretty well). <P>------------------<BR>Keith||||reg||12
Z||000004||revin||11-19-2001||08:23 AM||||Pull wires off ONE at a time.and replace them as soon as you pull one off!||||reg||1
